    <!-- Unit Overview -->
    <section class="welcome-section">
        <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-compass section-icon"></i> Unit Overview</h2>
        <p>The Internal Assessment (IA) focuses on the Iterative Cycle of software development. It moves beyond simple coding to encompass the full computational thinking process: identifying a human need, designing a robust solution, building complex logic, and critically evaluating the result against measurable success criteria.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Syllabus Links -->
    <section class="content-section">
        <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-bookmark section-icon"></i> What You'll Learn</h2>
        <div class="learning-points">
            <ul>
                <li>
                    Criterion A: Problem specification (measurable requirements) and Stakeholder identification (~300 words).
                </li>
                <li>
                    Criterion B: Planning, decomposition of the problem, and a chronology of steps (GANTT/Agile) (~150 words).
                </li>
                <li>
                    Criterion C: System overview (UML/Flowcharts), UI design, and a comprehensive testing strategy (~150 words).
                </li>
                <li>
                    Criterion D: Development (algorithmic complexity, implementation of data structures) and the 5-minute video demonstration (~1000 words).
                </li>
                <li>
                    Criterion E: Evaluation of success criteria and recommendations for future improvement (~400 words).
                </li>
                <li>
                    Appendices: Full source code and authentication documentation.
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </section>

